{
  "title": "Aamal of the 21st Night of Ramazan",
  "data": "Acts of the Night\nPerform the [Common Aamal at Each of the Three Qadr Nights](AA29). Ghusl and staying up the whole night in worship are especially stressed tonight and on the 23rd night.\nThese acts include visiting [Imam al-Husayn (a.s.)](G14), a two-unit prayer with [Surah al-Fatihah](A5) once and [Surah al-Tawheed](A116) seven times in each unit, placing the Qur'an on the head with its dua, and [Dua Jawshan Kabir](E29).\nSpending these nights in studying religious knowledge is also recommended.\nFrom this night on, recite the duas of the [Last Ten Nights of Ramazan](AA32). Ghusl on each of these nights and i'tikaf in the mosque are recommended.\nInvoke blessings on the Holy Prophet and his Household as often as you can tonight, and curse those who wronged the Ahl al-Bayt and the killer of Amir al-Mu'minin (a.s.).",
  "tabs": [
    "Dua of Sayyid Ibn Baqi\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nO Allah, (please) bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاقْسِمْ لِي حِلْمًا يَسُدُّ عَنِّيْ بَابَ الْجَهْلِ\nWAQSIM LEE HILMAN YASUDDU A'NNEE BAABAL JAHL\nand decide for me forbearance that blocks the door to ignorance against me,\nوَهُدًى تَمُنُّ بِهٖ عَلَيَّ مِنْ كُلِّ ضَلَالَةٍ\nWA HUDAN TAMUNNU BIHEE A'LAYYA MIN KULLI DALAALAH\nguidance that You confer upon me against any item of straying off,\nوَغِنًى تَسُدُّ بِهٖ عَنِّيْ بَابَ كُلِّ فَقْرٍ\nWA GHINAN TASUDDU BIHEE A'NNEE BAABA KULLI FAQR\naffluence that blocks the door to all poverty against me,\nوَقُوَّةً تَرُدُّ بِهَا عَنِّي كُلَّ ضَعْفٍ\nWA QUWWATAN TARUDDU BIHAA A'NNEE KULLA DA'F\npower due to which You repel any weakness from me,\nوَعِزًّا تُكْرِمُنِيْ بِهٖ عَنْ كُلِّ ذُلٍّ\nWA I'ZZAN TUKRIMUNEE BIHEE A'N KULLI DHULL\nmight with which You honor me against all humiliation,\nوَرِفْعَةً تَرْفَعُنِيْ بِهَا عَنْ كُلِّ ضَعَةٍ\nWA RIF'ATAN TARFA'UNEE BIHAA A'N KULLI DA'AH\nsublimity through which You exalt me against all humbleness,\nوَاَمْنًا تَرُدُّ بِهٖ عَنِّيْ كُلَّ خَوْفٍ\nWA AMNAN TARUDDU BIHEE A'NNEE KULLA KHAWF\nsecurity through which You protect me against any fear,\nوَعَافِيَةً تَسْتُرُنِي بِهَا عَنْ كُلِّ بَلَاۤءٍ\nWA A'AFIYATAN TASTURUNEE BIHAA A'N KULLI BALAA'\nwellbeing by which You cover me against any ailment,\nوَعِلْمًا تَفْتَحُ لِيْ بِهٖ كُلَّ يَقِيْنٍ\nWA I'LMAN TAFTAHOO LEE BIHEE KULLA YAQEEN\nknowledge due to which You open before me all certitude,\nوَيَقِيْنًا تُذْهِبُ بِهٖ عَنِّيْ كُلَّ شَكٍّ\nWA YAQEENAN TUDH-HIBU BIHEE A'NNEE KULLA SHAKK\ncertitude due to which You remove from me any doubt,\nوَدُعَاۤءً تَبْسُطُ لِيْ بِهِ الْاِجَابَةَ فِيْ هٰذِهِ اللَّيْلَةِ وَفِي هٰذِهِ السَّاعَةِ\nWA DU'AA'AN TABSUTU LEE BIHIL IJAABATA FEE HAADHIHIL LAYLATI WA FEE HAADHIHIS SAA'AH\nprayer through which You expand Your response to me at this very night and at this very hour,\nالسَّاعَةِ السَّاعَةِ السَّاعَةِ يَا كَرِيْمُ\nAS-SAA'ATIS SAA'ATIS SAA'ATI YAA KAREEM\nthis very hour, this very hour, this very hour, O All-generous,\nوَخَوْفًا تَنْشُرُ لِيْ بِهٖ كُلَّ رَحْمَةٍ\nWA KHAWFAN TANSHURU LEE BIHEE KULLA RAHMAH\napprehension due to which You spread over me all items of mercy,\nوَعِصْمَةً تَحُوْلُ بِهَا بَيْنِيْ وَبَيْنَ الذُّنُوْبِ\nWA I'SMATAN TAHOOLU BIHAA BAYNEE WA BAYNADH DHUNOOB\nand shelter due to which You intervene between my sins and me,\nحَتَّى اُفْلِحَ بِہَا عِنْدَ الْمَعْصُوْمِيْنَ عِنْدَكَ\nHATTAA UFLIHA BIHAA I'NDAL MA'SOOMEENA I'NDAK\nso that I shall succeed in the view of the Infallible ones with You,\nبِرَحْمَتِكَ يَآ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ\nBIRAHMATIKA YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nin the name of Your mercy, O most Merciful of all those who show mercy.",
    "Imam al-Sadiq (a.s.)'s Dua in Sajdah\nAfter the Fajr prayer and its taqibaat, go into sajdah and recite:\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُقَلِّبَ الْقُلُوْبِ وَالْاَبْصَارِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUQALLIBAL QULOOBI WAL ABSAAR\nThere is no god save You, the Transformer of hearts and sights,\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ خالِقَ الْخَلْقِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA KHAALIQAL KHALQ\nThere is no god save You, the Creator of the creatures,\nبِلَا حاجَةٍ فِيكَ اِلَيْهِمْ\nBILAA HAAJATIN FEEKA ILAYHIM\nWhile You do not need them.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُبْدِئَ الْخَلْقِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUBDI'AL KHALQ\nThere is no god save You, the Originator of the creation.\nوَلَا يَنْقُصُ مِنْ مُلْكِكَ شَيْءٌ\nWA LAA YANQUSU MIN MULKIKA SHAY'\nAnd nothing of creation decreases any of Your Kingdom.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ بَاعِثَ مَنْ فِي الْقُبُورِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA BAA'ITHA MAN FIL QUBOOR\nThere is no god save You, the Resurrector of those who are in graves.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُدَبِّرَ الْاُمُورِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUDABBIRAL UMOOR\nThere is no god save You, the Manager of all affairs.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ دَيَّانَ الدِّيْنِ وَجَبَّارَ الْجَبَابِرَةِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA DAYYAANAD DEENI WA JABBAARAL JABAABIRAH\nThere is no god save You, the Judge of the religion and the most Omnipotent of all those who claim omnipotence.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُجْرِيَ الْمَاءِ فِي الصَّخْرَةِ الصَّمَّاءِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUJRIYAL MAA'I FIS SAKHRATIS SAMMAA'\nThere is no god save You. It is You Who causes water to flow in hard rocks.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُجْرِيَ الْمَاءِ فِي النَّباتِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUJRIYAL MAA'I FIN NABAAT\nThere is no god save You. It is You Who causes water to flow in plants.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُكَوِّنَ طَعْمِ الثِّمارِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUKAWWINA TA'MITH THIMAAR\nThere is no god save You, the Maker of the flavors of fruits.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُحْصِيَ عَدَدِ الْقَطْرِ وَمَا تَحْمِلُهُ السَّحابُ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUHSIYA A'DADIL QATRI WA MAA TAHMILUHUS SAHAAB\nThere is no god save You. It is You Who keeps count of the number of the drops of rain and what is loaded by the clouds.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُحْصِيَ عَدَدِ ما تَجْرِي بِهِ الرِّياحُ فِي الْهَواءِ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUHSIYA A'DADI MAA TAJREE BIHIR REEHU FIL HAWAA'\nThere is no god save You. It is You Who keeps count of the number of what the wind carry in the air.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُحْصِيَ مَا فِي الْبِحَارِ مِنْ رَطْبٍ وَيَابِسٍ\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUHSIYA MAA FIL BIHAARI MIN RATBIN WA YAABIS\nThere is no god save You. It is You Who keeps count of what is there in oceans—the wet and the dry.\nلَا اِلٰهَ اِلَّا اَنْتَ مُحْصِيَ ما يَدُبُّ فِي ظُلُمَاتِ الْبِحَارِ وَفِي اَطْباقِ الثَّرى\nLAA ILAAHA ILLAA ANTA MUHSIYA MAA YADUBBU FEE ZULUMAATIL BIHAARI WA FEE ATBAAQITH THARAA\nThere is no god save You. It is You Who keeps count of whatever creeps in the darknesses of oceans and in the layers of the earth.\nاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي سَمَّيْتَ بِهٖ نَفْسَكَ\nAS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE SAMMAYTA BIHEE NAFSAK\nI beseech You by Your Name that You have used for Yourself\nاَوِ اسْتَاْثَرْتَ بِهٖ فِي عِلْمِ الْغَيْبِ عِنْدَكَ\nAWIS TA'THARTA BIHEE FEE I'LMIL GHAYBI I'NDAK\nOr You have stored for Yourself in the hidden knowledge of You.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِكُلِّ اسْمٍ سَمَّاكَ بِهٖ اَحَدٌ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BIKULLIS MIN SAMMAAKA BIHEE AHADUN MIN KHALQIK\nAnd I beseech You by every name that is ascribed to You by any of Your created beings:\nمِنْ نَبِيٍّ اَوْ صِدِّيقٍ اَوْ شَهِيدٍ اَوْ اَحَدٍ مِنْ مَلَائِكَتِكَ\nMIN NABIYYIN AW SIDDEEQIN AW SHAHEEDIN AW AHADIN MIN MALAA'IKATIK\nSuch as the Prophets, the veracious ones, the martyrs, or any of Your angels.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِاسْمِكَ الَّذِي اِذا دُعِيْتَ بِهٖ اَجَبْتَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BISMIKAL LADHEE IDHAA DU'EETA BIHEE AJABT\nAnd I beseech You by Your Name that You answer anyone who beseeches You by it,\nوَاِذا سُئِلْتَ بِهٖ اَعْطَيْتَ\nWA IDHAA SU'ILTA BIHEE A'TAYT\nAnd You respond to anyone who asks You by it.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِحَقِّكَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ صَلَواتُكَ عَلَيْهِمْ وَبَرَكاتُكَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BIHAQQIKA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIHEE SALAWAATUKA A'LAYHIM WA BARAKAATUK\nAnd I beseech You in the name of the duty that is incumbent upon Muhammad and his Household—Your blessings and benedictions be upon them—toward You,\nوَبِحَقِّهِمُ الَّذِي اَوْجَبْتَهٗ عَلٰى نَفْسِكَ\nWA BIHAQQIHIMUL LADHEE AWJABTAHOO A'LAA NAFSIK\nAnd by the duty that You have made incumbent upon Yourself toward them,\nوَاَنَلْتَهُمْ بِهٖ فَضْلَكَ\nWA ANALTAHUM BIHEE FADLAK\nAnd through which You granted them Your favors,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ عَبْدِكَ وَرَسُولِكَ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN A'BDIKA WA RASOOLIK\n(please) bless Muhammad, Your servant and Your Messenger:\nاَلدَّاعِي اِلَيْكَ بِاِذْنِكَ\nAD-DAA'EE ILAYKA BI-IDHNIK\nThe caller to You by Your permission,\nوَسِراجِكَ السَّاطِعِ بَيْنَ عِبادِكَ\nWA SIRAAJIKAS SAATI'I BAYNA I'BAADIK\nAnd Your incandescent lantern from among Your servants\nفِي اَرْضِكَ وَسَمَائِكَ\nFEE ARDIKA WA SAMAA'IK\nIn Your lands and Your heavens,\nوَجَعَلْتَهٗ رَحْمَةً لِلْعَالَمِيْنَ\nWA JA'ALTAHOO RAHMATAN LIL A'ALAMEEN\nAnd he whom You made mercy for the peoples,\nوَنُوراً اسْتَضاءَ بِهِ الْمُؤْمِنُونَ\nWA NOORANIS TADAA'A BIHIL MU'MINOON\nAnd light through whom the believers have obtained their light;\nفَبَشَّرَنَا بِجَزِيلِ ثَوابِكَ\nFABASHSHARANAA BIJAZEELI THAWAABIK\nHe this conveyed to us the good tidings about Your abundant reward\nوَاَنْذَرَنَا الْاَلِيمَ مِنْ عَذَابِكَ\nWA ANDHARANAL ALEEMA MIN A'DHAABIK\nAnd also warned us against Your painful chastisement.\nاَشْهَدُ اَنَّهٗ قَدْ جَاءَ بِالْحَقِّ مِنْ عِنْدِ الْحَقِّ وَصَدَّقَ الْمُرْسَلِينَ\nASH-HADU ANNAHOO QAD JAA'A BIL HAQQI MIN I'NDIL HAQQI WA SADDAQAL MURSALEEN\nI bear witness that he carried to us the truth from the True God, and he verified the Messengers.\nوَاَشْهَدُ اَنَّ الَّذِينَ كَذَّبُوهُ ذَائِقُو الْعَذَابِ الْاَلِيمِ\nWA ASH-HADU ANNAL LADHEENA KADHDHABOOHU DHAA'IQUL A'DHAABIL ALEEM\nAnd I bear witness that those who belied him shall certainly taste the painful chastisement.\nاَسْاَلُكَ يا اللهُ يا اَللهُ يا اَللهُ\nAS'ALUKA YALLAAHU YAA ALLAAHU YAA ALLAAH\nI beseech You, O Allah; O Allah; O Allah;\nيا رَبَّاهُ يا رَبَّاهُ يا رَبَّاهُ\nYAA RABBAAHU YAA RABBAAHU YAA RABBAAH\nO our God; O our God; O our God;\nيا سَيِّدِي يا سَيِّدِي يا سَيِّدِي\nYAA SAYYIDEE YAA SAYYIDEE YAA SAYYIDEE\nO my Master; O my Master; O my Master;\nيَا مَوْلَايَ يَا مَوْلَايَ يَا مَوْلَايَ\nYAA MAWLAAYA YAA MAWLAAYA YAA MAWLAAY\nO my Lord; O my Lord; O my Lord.\nاَسْاَلُكَ فِي هٰذِهِ الْغَداةِ اَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nAS'ALUKA FEE HAADHIHIL GHADAATI AN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\nI beseech You in this early morning to bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاَنْ تَجْعَلَنِي مِنْ اَوْفَرِ عِبادِكَ وَسَائِلِيْكَ نَصِيْباً\nWA AN TAJ'ALANEE MIN AWFARI I'BAADIKA WA SAA'ILEEKA NASEEBAA\nAnd to include me with Your servants and beseechers upon whom You confer the most abundant of Your rewards,\nوَاَنْ تَمُنَّ عَلَيَّ بِفَكَاكِ رَقَبَتِي مِنَ النَّارِ\nWA AN TAMUNNA A'LAYYA BIFAKAAKI RAQABATEE MINAN NAAR\nAnd to confer upon me with releasing me from Hellfire,\nيا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO the most Merciful of all those who show mercy.\nوَاَسْاَلُكَ بِجَمِيْعِ ما سَاَلْتُكَ وَمَا لَمْ اَسْاَلْكَ مِنْ عَظِيْمِ جَلَالِكَ\nWA AS'ALUKA BIJAMEE'I MAA SA'ALTUKA WA MAA LAM AS'ALKA MIN A'ZEEMI JALAALIK\nAnd I beseech You to settle for me all that which I asked from You and also all that which I did not ask from You; that which belongs to Your splendid majesty,\nمَا لَوْ عَلِمْتُهٗ لَسَاَلْتُكَ بِهٖ\nMAA LAW A'LIMTUHOO LASA'ALTUKA BIH\nThat which I would ask from You if I knew it,\nاَنْ تُصَلِّيَ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاَهْلِ بَيْتِهٖ\nAN TUSALLIYA A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AHLI BAYTIH\n(and I beseech You to) send blessings upon Muhammad and his Household,\nوَاَنْ تَاْذَنَ لِفَرَجِ مَنْ بِفَرَجِهٖ فَرَجُ اَوْلِيَائِكَ وَاَصْفِيَائِكَ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ\nWA AN TA'DHANA LIFARAJI MAN BIFARAJIHEE FARAJU AWLIYAA'IKA WA ASFIYAA'IKA MIN KHALQIK\nAnd to permit the Relief of him whose relief achieves the relief of Your intimate servants and Your select ones from among Your created beings,\nوَبِهٖ تُبِيْدُ الظَّالِمِيْنَ وَتُهْلِكُهُمْ\nWA BIHEE TUBEEDUZ ZAALIMEENA WA TUHLIKUHUM\nAnd through whom You will terminate and eradicate the oppressors.\nعَجِّلْ ذٰلِكَ يا رَبَّ الْعَالَمينَ\nA'JJIL DHAALIKA YAA RABBAL A'ALAMEEN\n(Please) hasten that, O the Lord of the worlds.\nوَاَعْطِنِي سُؤْلِي يَا ذَا الْجَلَالِ وَالْاِكْرامِ\nWA A'TINEE SU'LEE YAA DHAL JALAALI WAL IKRAAM\nAnd (please) grant me my requests, O the Lord of majesty and honor,\nفِي جَمِيعِ ما سَاَلْتُكَ لِعاجِلِ الدُّنْيا وَاٰجِلِ الْاٰخِرَةِ\nFEE JAMEE'I MAA SA'ALTUKA LI'AAJILID DUNYAA WA AAJILIL AAKHIRAH\nAs regarding all that which I have asked You from my needs for this worldly life and the Hereafter.\nيَا مَنْ هُوَ اَقْرَبُ اِلَيَّ مِنْ حَبْلِ الْوَرِيدِ اَقِلْنِي عَثْرَتِي\nYAA MAN HUWA AQRABU ILAYYA MIN HABLIL WAREEDI AQILNEE A'THRATEE\nO He Who is nearer to me than my life-vein: (Please) overlook my slips,\nوَاَقِلْنِي بِقَضَاءِ حَوَائِجِي\nWA AQILNEE BIQADAA'I HAWAA'IJEE\nAnd revive me through settling my needs.\nيَا خَالِقِي وَيَا رَازِقي وَيَا بَاعِثِي\nYAA KHAALIQEE WA YAA RAAZIQEE WA YAA BAA'ITH\nO my Creator; O the Source of my sustenance; O my Resurrector;\nوَيَا مُحْيِي عِظَامِي وَهِيَ رَمِيْمٌ\nWA YAA MUHYEE I'ZAAMEE WA HIYA RAMEEM\nO He Who shall give life to my bones when they are rotten:\nصَلِّ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِ مُحَمَّدٍ\nSALLI A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALI MUHAMMAD\n(Please do) bless Muhammad and the Household of Muhammad,\nوَاسْتَجِبْ لِي دُعَائِي يَا اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِينَ\nWASTAJIB LEE DU'AA'EE YAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nAnd respond to my prayer; O the most Merciful of all those who show mercy."
